The error he's getting is probable "call to undefined dynalink". This can 
happen if he has two versions of the Quick Time for Windows libraries on his 
system. Myst installs it's own version of the Quick Time libraries on your 
system. One thing you might try is to delete all files starting with the 
letter 'q' from your Myst installation directory, reboot, and retry the game. 
You may not have to reboot to retry the game. It's been a while since I 
played the game and had this problem myself. Good luck.



